::PC_U05_L04_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L04_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.PA.1
Question:
Which statement is correct about circles as conic sections?
{
~A. The radius is always the number on the right side of the equation.#This choice misses the key structure of the lesson. Return to the definition and identify the required feature before choosing an answer.
=B. A circle is the set of points the same distance from a center.#Correct. A circle is defined by a center and a constant radius.
~C. The center is ignored when graphing a circle.#This choice misses the key structure of the lesson. Return to the definition and identify the required feature before choosing an answer.
~D. A circle cannot come from slicing a cone.#This choice misses the key structure of the lesson. Return to the definition and identify the required feature before choosing an answer.
}
